# 1.75 Carat Marquise Diamond Price ({{year}}): Why 1.74ct Saves $900

![Three loose 1.75 carat marquise natural diamonds held in jeweller tweezers against a soft grey backdrop as the DiamondCritics featured image for the {{year}} 1.75 carat marquise diamond price sub-threshold buying guide](/images/1-75-carat-marquise-diamond-price.jpg "1.75 Carat Marquise Diamond Price Why 1.74ct Saves 900")

## TL;DR — 1.75 Carat Marquise Diamond Price in One Scroll

**1.75 carat marquise diamond price** starts at **[$1,638](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29885965?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** for IGI E-VVS2 Excellent Cut lab-grown — four identical stones at this exact price. Natural starts at **[$12,804](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29498926?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** for GIA G-SI2 Very Good. The 1.74ct sub-threshold trick saves roughly **$900** vs an equivalent 1.75ct on natural — crossing the quarter-carat tier line triggers a 7–10% price jump for 0.01ct the eye never measures.

**The 3 things to know (in order):**

- **1.74ct saves $900 natural.** A 1.74ct marquise is 12.9 × 6.45 mm. A 1.75ct is 13.0 × 6.5 mm. 0.1 mm nobody can see. The tier jump at 1.75 adds 7–10%.
- **Natural inventory is paper-thin.** Only 2 certified natural stones at 1.75ct — both SI1/SI2 clarity. Eye-clean verification mandatory before buying.
- **Lab at $1,638 is the whole value play.** Four IGI E-VVS2 stones at the floor is a configuration you can't match on any adjacent carat tier.

→ Our pick: **[IGI E-VVS2 Ideal Cut at $1,638](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30162971?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — top-grade spec, Ideal cut label, $1,638 leaves $3,000+ for a serious platinum setting.

**Priority:** at 1.75ct, the natural market is too thin and too SI-heavy to recommend without reservations. Lab is the honest play. The 1.74ct sub-threshold trick on natural is only valuable if you have $12k+ and want GIA + natural specifically. Full breakdown below.

## Expert Summary

1.75 carat marquise diamond price sits in a $1,638–$13,564 band in current certified market inventory. The lab floor is $1,638 for IGI E-VVS2 Excellent — four identical stones. Natural inventory is only 2 stones ($12,804 G-SI2 VG and $13,564 E-SI1 VG) — both SI clarity, both Very Good cut. The size face-up is 13.0 × 6.5 mm at a 2.00 length-to-width ratio — reads as a 2.25ct round diamond face-up.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a GIA-certified diamond expert. 1.75ct marquise is one of the thinnest-inventory carat tiers in the entire marquise market because cutters do not target it — they aim for 1.5ct or 2.0ct. The 1.74ct sub-threshold trick lets you dodge the quarter-carat tier premium without changing how the stone looks on the hand. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every carat tier.

This guide covers the full certified market audit at 1.75ct marquise natural (2 GIA stones) and lab (8 IGI stones), the 1.74ct Sub-Threshold Jump concept, the SI Clarity Trap at 1.75ct natural, the Lab Quadruplet framework, and the setting math that fits inside the $5,500–$9,000 total ring target. All prices verified against live certified inventory. Pricing presented as independent market research.

